cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Agent RCA Bench
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, its protocol, or its published measurements, please
  cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dennis
    family-names: Zhuang
    email: xzhuang@greptime.com
    affiliation: Greptime
    orcid: null
repository-code: https://github.com/GreptimeTeam/agent-rca-bench
url: https://rca-bench.greptime.com
abstract: >-
  A paired benchmark measuring how the observability interface behind a large
  language model agent changes root cause analysis. Protocol v34 compares three
  interfaces on identical incidents, prompts, models and budgets: Prometheus
  with Loki and Tempo through their native query APIs, GreptimeDB over read-only
  SQL and PromQL, and that same GreptimeDB with its Semantic Graph. It reports
  diagnosis accuracy, investigation work, and cost, with two comparison families
  specified and frozen before any run and Holm-corrected separately. The
  measurement is designed to report negative results: the semantic-layer family
  returned none of its eight endpoints significant.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - root cause analysis
  - observability
  - large language model agent
  - opentelemetry
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-04'
references:
  - type: data
    title: OpenRCA
    notes: >-
      Discovery micro-benchmark cases. Declares CC BY-NC 4.0.
    url: https://github.com/microsoft/OpenRCA
  - type: data
    title: OpenRCA2 ops-lite
    notes: >-
      End-to-end service cases and Graph-retrieval micro cases. The dataset card
      declares Apache-2.0 while the paper declares CC-BY-SA 4.0.
    url: https://huggingface.co/datasets/anon-ops/ops-lite
  - type: data
    title: RCA100
    notes: >-
      End-to-end infrastructure-node cases. Declares CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and
      requires attribution to its dataset paper.
    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.29193
